1. THE CASE AND THE ACCEPTANCE (RECORD)
   the breaker's held 23.93 A from 76.25 C (record l9stk B-P2; record l8p's breaker), the band 9.16 K, R17 5 mOhm (2.863 W nominal) its
     coupling into a junction at most 1.0 K/W (E-1), the budget 64.59 K for the FETs and R17's coupling (150 C less 76.25 C and 9.16 K)
   E-1's bar (L4-E11 E11-29): each FET's (Zself + 2 Zmut) at most 40.78 K/W; the worst-split figure's limit 73.75 K over the air; E11-29's
     design target Zw at most 37.59 K/W with R17's coupling at most 0.29 K/W; record l9stk's even-split bar 45.88 K/W
   path 2's relaxation (record l8p 10c): the FETs carry current at most 43.8 ms in every 0.154 s or more; the RC hold's least 0.110 s
   M-A's acceptance (register row L4A-66; decision L4E11-FET-D2): every series part inside its PRINTED limits held indefinitely at 23.93 A
     from 76.25 C, the battery FETs at most 150 C on the printed Zth and RDS(on) at temperature; a typical FAILS

2. M-A, THE GUARD'S OWN PARTS: Q39, Q40 AND Q42 (BUK6Y10-30P), THEIR POUR AND VIAS, R17
   2a. the FETs (PRINTED, Nexperia 17 April 2020): RDS(on) max 10 mOhm at -10 V and 25 C (p.6), 16 at 175 C, 25 at -4.5 V and 25 C;
       Rth(j-mb) 1.1 typ, 1.4 MAX K/W (p.5); Tj 175 C (p.3), its limit here 150 C
       the allowance at BATDRV's least -8.5 V and 150 C (INFERRED, two chords on printed maxima, E11-36): hot 1.5000 x drive 1.4091: 21.136 mOhm
       at 23.93 A: 1.3448 W a FET on the even split; 1.5130 W in the hottest on the worst split (one at R/2, 11.96 A, under the 13.5 A row)
       the hottest junction over its mounting base on the printed Rth(j-mb) MAXIMUM: 2.12 K (record l8p 12m: 2.12 K)
       the even-split bar on the budget: 45.90 K/W (record 45.88; record l4e11 round FET 45.90), the worst split's 40.80 K/W (record 40.78)
       the hottest junction held at 23.93 A: at E-1's bar 150.00 C (0.00 K under 150 C, by construction); at E11-29's design target 136.79 C
         (13.21 K under 150 C); at the design target the three reach 150 C only at 26.41 A held, over the breaker's 23.93 A (INFERRED, the
         150 C allowance kept at every current)
       the device's own figures are PRINTED maxima; the installed path (the pour, Zself and Zmut) is no maker's figure: it is E-1's bar,
         a layout requirement that E11-29's coupon decides (CONDITIONAL), and the allowance at -8.5 V rests on E11-36's chords; the three
         as a set rest on E-05 (TI's 5 nF, record l4e11 round FET)
   2b. the printed Zth curve, Fig. 4 (READING of its vector paths; 8 curves, labelled duty 1 to 0.01; no single-pulse curve):
       duty 1: 1.178 K/W at 10 us, 1.291 at 10 ms, 1.306 at 0.98 s; the largest of any curve 1.360 K/W
       the curve never reaches the printed Rth(j-mb) maximum 1.4 K/W and sits over its typical 1.1: it is not a maximum; the figure says
         neither typical nor maximum, so this record classes it TYPICAL (never a limit); a bound on it is refused (section 5)
   2c. the pour and the vias (MODEL: decision 35's conductor model in record l9stk; the limits are the parts' printed ones):
       the band carrying 23.93 A: 9.16 K over the air, 85.41 C, against board A's band limit 105 C as fitted (125 C with the blade's
         silver plating pinned): WITHIN; the barrel field at R17 (16 of 0.4 mm) 0.75 A a barrel, 7.62 K: WITHIN
       CH_BATQ (R17 to the three) is a one-face hop at the parts' lands, inside E-1's installed path: E11-29's coupon carries the band and
         R17 in place; the laminate's own limit is NOT HELD (L9-STACKUPS 14.3)
   2d. R17 (PRINTED, ROHM GMR100 HJ, rev. 006E, 5 March 2026; GMR100HJAAFD5L00 = 5 mOhm, JA, F 1 %; first read by this record):
       rated 7 W at a terminal temperature Tk of 70 C, derated to 0 at 170 C (Fig. 1), or 5 W at Tk 110 C, derated to 0 at 170 C (Fig. 2);
       operating -65 to +170 C; TCR 0 to +50 ppm/C, printed for 20 to 60 C only (above 60 C ASSUMED to continue)
       at 23.93 A on its printed maximum 5.0500 mOhm: 2.892 W at 60 C, 2.902 W at Tk 128.5 C
       the lower of the two printed derating lines admits it to Tk 128.5 C (Fig. 2 alone would admit 135.2 C): R17's terminals may rise
         43.1 K over the band's 85.41 C, so its terminal-to-band path at most 14.9 K/W: a LAYOUT condition, read on E11-29's coupon with
         R17 dissipating in place; at the band's own temperature R17 is at 58 % of its derated power
       record l9stk's '5 W printed at 25 C, derating NOT HELD (E-6)' is answered by the sheet: E-6 for R17 becomes the terminal reading above

