4. WHICH ROWS THE GUARD EVER PROTECTED (INFERRED)
   the guard senses only board A's battery-FET pour: no trip under 127.8 C at its die, surely tripped from 132.2 C (record l8p 12m)
   with the pour at E11-29's design target, at the blades' rerated 23.10 A held the hottest FET reads 132.64 C and its mounting base 130.67 C;
     the guard's die is no hotter than the copper it sits on (its own heating 0.008 K, record l8p 9 (a)), so its trip is not assured
     there: a held overload from 23.10 A to the breaker's 23.93 A can persist with the guard intact, and the rows of section 3 read the
     same with or without it; only section 2's rows (the parts on the pour it senses) depend on it
   page 12o's exposure, 'the battery FETs reach 150 C held at 20.53 A', is record l9stk's PAIR figure (its section 2: 20.53 A, the pair on
     the then 33.12 K/W target); for the drawn three at E-1's bar the figure is 23.93 A, the breaker's own most limit

5. L4A-65: PATH 2'S RETRY ENERGY ALONE (path 1 lost; current up to the breaker's 23.93 A; 76.25 C air)
   the train (RECORD, record l8p 10c): on at most 43.8 ms, off at least 0.110 s, period at least 0.154 s, duty at most 0.284
   the rise per on-time over the mounting base, hottest FET at 1.5130 W: at most 2.12 K on the printed Rth(j-mb) MAXIMUM (a passive
     network's transient impedance never exceeds its steady resistance, so Zth(j-mb) at 43.8 ms is at most 1.4 K/W) (INFERRED, PRINTED)
   Fig. 4 at 43.8 ms (READING): 1.357 K/W on duty 0.30, 1.354 on 0.10, 1.357 at the train's duty: 2.05 K, class TYPICAL:
     REFUSED as a limit (Fig. 4 at 43.8 ms: a TYPICAL figure is not a limit)
   the steady periodic peak: any on and off pattern whose current never exceeds 23.93 A heats every junction at most as the same current
     held does (superposition on a passive thermal network; the RDS(on) at its 150 C allowance at every instant), so the peak is at most
     the held state: 150.00 C at E-1's bar, 136.79 C at E11-29's design target: BOUNDED against 150 C on printed device maxima, CONDITIONAL
     on E11-29 (the pour), E11-36 (the allowance) and E-05 (the three), as section 2a; bounded on the typical curve instead: FAILS
   the train's mean loss is at most 0.284 of the held one; no credit is taken for it (the pour's own transient is no maker's figure)
   currents over 23.93 A are single events outside the train, judged in their records: a fault's onset up to the breaker's 50.59 A for
     at most 16.5 us, after which the -1 latches off and a restart into the short is power-limited (record l9stk 15.3, its table); the
     docking pulse, 242.9 A once per docking (L4-E11 16d, E11-30)
   the breaker's own FETs under the train: each restart is judged under DD-8's restart inhibit (record l8p round 2, l9stk 15.4b),
     not here; board P's Q1 and Q2 under the train: at most their held row (section 3f), by the same superposition

6. VERDICTS
   the guard's own parts (section 2): the three FETs HOLD 23.93 A indefinitely at 150.00 C at E-1's bar (136.79 C at the design target),
     CONDITIONAL on E11-29, E11-36 and E-05; the pour and the vias WITHIN on the model; R17 WITHIN its printed derating while its
     terminals stay at or under 128.5 C (CONDITIONAL, read on E11-29's coupon)
   every other series part (section 3): the three 25 A blades OVER their printed rerated current by 3.6 % (0.83 A) at the air;
     NOT SHOWN on printed maxima: board P's Q1, Q2, Q109, Q101, Q102 (hot RDS(on) typical only), R10, R101 and R102 (no derating held),
     the wires (no sheet), the pins' split (E-4); WITHIN on printed current: the holders, the XT60 (its rise INFERRED), the pins evenly
   so M-A's acceptance as the register writes it ('every series part inside its PRINTED limits') is NOT MET on printed figures: the
     blades by 0.83 A, the rest NOT SHOWN; each of those rows is independent of the guard (section 4), so none is HO-A's consequence
   L4A-65 (HO-B): BOUNDED on printed device maxima at the held state (150.00 C at the bar); FAILS on the typical curve, as it must
   what M-A closes once checked (L4A-69): HO-A's consequence for the parts the guard protects (the three FETs hold the breaker's most
     limit, so a latent guard failure removes no protection they need) and HO-B (no retry exceeds a current they hold); the guard
     stays as defence in depth; CONDITIONAL on E-05, E11-29 (with R17's terminal reading) and E11-36
   M-B's entry condition (decision L4E11-FET-D2): (1) and (2) not met (E11-29, E11-36 and E-05 unanswered, none refused); (3) not met for
     the guard's parts; the blades' row is a part over its printed limit, but the guard does not assure its protection, nor would M-B:
     it enters C-PROT rev 1's re-evaluation (L4A-67), not M-B

7. PREDICATES
   the allowance reproduces record l4e11's 21.136 mOhm from the printed rows                                              yes
   the even-split bar reproduces record l9stk's within 0.1 %                                                              yes
   the worst split's bar reproduces E-1's 40.78 K/W within 0.1 %                                                          yes
   the three hold the breaker's most limit at or under 150 C at E-1's bar                                                 yes
   at E11-29's design target the three reach 150 C only above the breaker's most limit                                    yes
   the junction's lead over its mounting base is 2.12 K on the printed Rth(j-mb) maximum                                  yes
   Fig. 4's curves never reach the printed Rth(j-mb) maximum (the curve is not a maximum)                                 yes
   a bound read on Fig. 4 is refused as a limit                                                                           yes
   R17 is within ROHM's lower derating line at the band's temperature                                                     yes
   R17's admitted terminal temperature comes from the lower of the two printed lines                                      yes
   the 25 A blades are over their printed rerated current at the 76.25 C air                                              yes
   the rerating line passes 100 % within 0.5 % at 25 C                                                                    yes
   the 18 A service is within the blades' rerated current                                                                 yes
   a 30 A blade would carry the held current within its rerating                                                          yes
   the LM5069's printed VCL span cannot fit the 18.32 A least and the blades' rerated most                                yes
   the pins' split ratio for 9 A at the held current is under 25 A's 0.593                                                yes
   the XT60 is within its printed 30 A                                                                                    yes
   at the blades' rerated current the guard's sure trip is not reached on the design target's pour                        yes
   page 12o's 20.53 A is record l9stk's pair figure                                                                       yes
   path 2's on-time and the RC hold make its period                                                                       yes
   the retry train's peak is bounded by the held state on printed device maxima                                           yes
